# Keyboard Behavior
Applies to any screen with text fields/forms. Does NOT apply to chat/messaging screens — see exception below.

## Dismiss the keyboard when:
- the user taps anywhere outside the field: wrap the screen's body in a GestureDetector with `onTap: () => FocusScope.of(context).unfocus()`, `behavior: HitTestBehavior.opaque` so taps on empty space register
- the user presses "Done"/submit on the keyboard: set `textInputAction: TextInputAction.done` (or `.next` if chaining to another field) and call `FocusScope.of(context).unfocus()` in `onEditingComplete` or `onFieldSubmitted`
- the user scrolls a scrollable containing the field: set `keyboardDismissBehavior: ScrollViewKeyboardDismissBehavior.onDrag` on the ListView/SingleChildScrollView/CustomScrollView

## Exception — chat/messaging screens
- do NOT auto-dismiss on scroll in a chat/message list — the user needs to keep typing while reviewing earlier messages
- do NOT dismiss on tap-outside if the tap target is the message list itself, since that's the primary interaction surface
- "Done"/send button behavior in chat should submit the message, not just dismiss the keyboard

## General
- every screen with a form: apply all three dismiss behaviors above by default unless it's identified as a chat/messaging screen
- multi-field forms: chain fields with `TextInputAction.next` + `FocusNode`s, only the last field uses `.done`
